 multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. For example, if $f(1)=g(1)=2,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1)+g(1) & =2+2 \\\\  & =4,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is not a polynomial from $B.$ So, $B$ is *not* closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, if $f(1)=2$ and $k=2,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kf(1) & =2\\cdot 2=4,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is not a polynomial from $B.$ So, $B$ is *not* closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is false, while statement IV is true. $B$ is *not* a subspace because it's not closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"IV only.\"" 13194139535468 true] [17592186350708 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350709 13194139535468 true] [17592186350708 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350710 13194139535468 true] [17592186350708 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350711 13194139535468 true] [17592186350708 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350712 13194139535468 true] [17592186350708 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350713 13194139535468 true] [17592186350708 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535468 true] [17592186350708 1041 "selection" 13194139535468 true] [17592186350708 1104 #edb/ref 17592186350712 13194139535468 true] [17592186350708 1110 #uuid "d9f26bff-a5ba-524f-83c7-c40abc798a89" 13194139535468 true] [17592186350709 1034 "I and IV only" 13194139535468 true] [17592186350709 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535468 true] [17592186350709 1111 #uuid "4d7ec20e-9590-5257-b6e6-4c1e9dd1bc96" 13194139535468 true] [17592186350710 1034 "II and IV only" 13194139535468 true] [17592186350710 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535468 true] [17592186350710 1111 #uuid "dc904574-4999-5913-95db-88609d9da83e" 13194139535468 true] [17592186350711 1034 "I, II, and III only" 13194139535468 true] [17592186350711 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535468 true] [17592186350711 1111 #uuid "537d219c-98b7-539d-b45b-2258da944335" 13194139535468 true] [17592186350712 1034 "IV 