aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}],$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1}+{A}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is not a matrix from $H.$ So, $H$ is *not* closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, if $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ and $k=2,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kA & =2[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is not a matrix from $H.$ So, $H$ is *not* closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is false, while statement IV is true. $H$ is a *not* subspace because it's not closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"IV only.\"" 13194139535468 true] [17592186350736 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350737 13194139535468 true] [17592186350736 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350738 13194139535468 true] [17592186350736 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350739 13194139535468 true] [17592186350736 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350740 13194139535468 true] [17592186350736 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350741 13194139535468 true] [17592186350736 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535468 true] [17592186350736 1041 "selection" 13194139535468 true] [17592186350736 1104 #edb/ref 17592186350741 13194139535468 true] [17592186350736 1110 #uuid "21d3a40c-4e52-5bbe-9c7e-ae124c2f2a68" 13194139535468 true] [17592186350737 1034 "I and IV only" 13194139535468 true] [17592186350737 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535468 true] [17592186350737 1111 #uuid "2708ddf5-06f6-546e-afba-c49565f9fdd4" 13194139535468 true] [17592186350738 1034 "II and IV only" 13194139535468 true] [17592186350738 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535468 true] [17592186350738 1111 #uuid "c4478e1e-e773-5ff9-875c-9ed499835d7b" 13194139535468 true] [17592186350739 1034 "I only" 13194139535468 true] [17592186350739 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535468 true] [17592186350739 1111 #uuid "140e46e0-21b0-5d9f-954d-3f554622d179" 13194139535468 true] [17592186350740 1034 "I, II, and III only" 13194139535468 true] [17592186350740 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535468 true] [17592186350740 1111 #uuid "67361646-174e-5340-b1ce-e24fa0a1735a" 13194139535468 true] [17592186350741 1034 "IV only" 13194139535468 true] [17592186350741 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535468 true] [17592186350741 1111 #uuid "857a864a-a246-56e2-80d9-ba304020a137" 13194139535468 true] [17592186350742 1017 #edb/ref 17592186350743 13194139535468 true] [17592186350742 1089 "q-94633" 13194139535468 true] [17592186350742 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535468 true] [17592186350742 1100 "Consider the vector space $C[0,1]$ of all continuous functions $f:[0,1]\\to R$ and its subset $Q$ containing all polynomials of degree exactly $2.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $Q$ is closed under function addition\n- $Q$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- $Q$ is a subspace of $C[0,1]$\n- $Q$ is **not** a subspace of $C[0,1]$" 13194139535468 true] [17592186350742 1113 #uuid "fc18f1a0-e2bd-52ed-93fe-4648ff2e2097" 13194139535468 true] [17592186350742 1145 "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. For example, if $f(x)={x}^{2}$ and $g(x)=-{x}^{2},$ then\n\n$$\nf(x)+g(x)={x}^{2}+(-{x}^{2})=0.\n$$\n\nSo, $Q$ is *not* closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, if $f(x)={x}^{2}$ and $k=0,$ then\n\n$$\nkf(x)=0\\cdot {x}^{2}=0.\n$$\n\n \nSo, $Q$ is *not* closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is false, while statement IV is true. $Q$ is *not* a subspace because it's not closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"IV only.\"" 13194139535468 true] [17592186350743 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350744 13194139535468 true] [17592186350743 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350745 13194139535468 true] [17592186350743 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350746 13194139535468 true] [17592186350743 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350747 13194139535468 true] [17592186350743 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350748 13194139535468 true] [17592186350743 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535468 true] [17592186350743 1041 "selection" 13194139535468 true] [17592186350743 1104 #edb/ref 17592186350748 13194139535468 true] [17592186350743 1110 #uuid "54274b23-7dcf-51bc-a83b-714784cb5b83" 13194139535468 true] [17592186350744 1034 "I and IV only" 13194139535468 true] [17592186350744 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535468 true] [17592186350744 1111 #uuid "a0c74a5f-b58f-5929-9579-48df8a7b4af9" 13194139535468 true] [17592186350745 1034 "II and IV only" 13194139535468 true] [17592186350745 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535468 true] [17592186350745 1111 #uuid "f3e7ca52-8deb-57c7-82fb-0096c905db96" 13194139535468 true] [17592186350746 1034 "I only" 13194139535468 true] [17592186350746 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535468 true] [17592186350746 1111 #uuid "2cf826a9-3e6f-5c25-a17d-07e9b4de2394" 13194139535468 true] [17592186350747 1034 "I, II, and III only" 13194139535468 true] [17592186350747 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535468 true] [17592186350747 1111 #uuid "479ae802-368f-5745-ab33-080d1d96351f" 13194139535468 true] [17592186350748 1034 "IV only" 13194139535468 true] [17592186350748 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535468 true] [17592186350748 1111 #uuid "097fe3c3-adf8-58ec-ab92-bf0d76267c13" 13194139535468 true] [17592186350749 1017 #edb/ref 17592186350750 13194139535468 true] [17592186350749 1089 "q-94642" 13194139535468 true] [17592186350749 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535468 true] [17592186350749 1100 "Consider the vector space $C[-2,2]$ of all continuous functions $f:[-2,2]\\to R$ and its subset $E$ containing all even functions.\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $E$ is closed under function addition\n- $E$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- $E$ is a subspace of $C[-2,2]$\n- $E$ is **not** a subspace of $C[-2,2]$\n\n*Hint: $f$ is even if $f(-x)=f(x)$ for all $x\\in [-2,2].$*" 13194139535468 true] [17592186350749 1113 #uuid "10bf265e-e38c-58b3-b176-163baf65aeab" 13194139535468 true] [17592186350749 1145 "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. If $f(x),g(x)\\in E,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f+g)(-x) & =f(-x)+g(-x) \\\\  & =f(x)+g(x) \\\\  & =(f+g)(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $E$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $f(x)\\in E$ and $k\\in R,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(kf)(-x) & =kf(-x) \\\\  & =kf(x) \\\\  & =(kf)(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $E$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is true, while statement IV is false. $E$ is a subspace because it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\"" 13194139535468 true] [17592186350750 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350751 13194139535468 true] [17592186350750 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350752 13194139535468 true] [17592186350750 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350753 13194139535468 true] [17592186350750 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350754 13194139535468 true] [17592186350750 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350755 13194139535468 true] [17592186350750 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535468 true] [17592186350750 1041 "selection" 13194139535468 true] [17592186350750 1104 #edb/ref 17592186350753 13194139535468 true] [17592186350750 1110 #uuid "347c020d-2c38-583d-90ea-b7a0303fd146" 13194139535468 true] [17592186350751 1034 "I and IV only" 13194139535468 true] [17592186350751 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535468 true] [17592186350751 1111 #uuid "59ca04ee-2415-550c-bba3-fbcc6b9c8730" 13194139535468 true] [175921